  "notes": "Living data file — the list of phrases that read as machine-generated drifts as models change. Update this file directly (or point at your own copy via --phrases-file / options.phrasesFile) rather than forking the package. Entries are matched case-insensitively with word boundaries for \"literal\" type, or as a raw regex for \"regex\" type. Grounded in the cited sources below, adapted for game dialogue/prose rather than transplanted verbatim: Wikipedia's list was written for detecting AI-written *encyclopedia articles*, a different register from terse dialogue, so several documented categories were deliberately excluded or down-weighted here rather than imported wholesale — see each entry's own `source`/`note`, and packages/prose/RESEARCH.md for the full reasoning, including what was left out and why (bare \"landscape\"/\"robust\"/\"valuable\"/\"key\"/\"crucial\" all have ordinary, legitimate meanings in fantasy-RPG prose specifically, so they're excluded as standalone words to avoid drowning real findings in false positives).",
  "sources": [
